{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>If a ransom is laid upon him.</b> This \"if\" is not conditional — it is like \"אִם כֶּסֶף תַּלְוֶה\" — meaning \"which\": this is its ruling, that the court lays a ransom upon him." "<b>And he shall give the redemption of his life.</b> The payment for the damage — these are the words of Rabbi Yishmael; Rabbi Akiva says: the payment of the one who caused damage (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:42.201773037Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}